From 07471e0db29cde93223316afa60aaff3e4c9e9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virt-ios <virt-ios@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:31:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] :new: Windows platform for the Vulkan crate (builds)

The Vulkan platform's OS layer on Windows, os/windows.rs and os/windows/,
so the library can run natively there and import guest pages into the
host GPU by pointer: WSL2 has no Vulkan driver for the host GPU and
reims-vgpu falls back to lavapipe there.

- reims-vgpu-winvm: Mach-style VM calls over Windows placeholders
  (VirtualAlloc2 / MapViewOfFile3 with MEM_REPLACE_PLACEHOLDER), at 4 KiB
  granularity, with a region map; 10 tests pass on Windows 11.
- vm.rs follows Linux's model (views of the files the backing table
  names), a section being the file; no dma-buf views, no budget.
- files/import/surface/host_ram start from Linux's, with dma-bufs, the
  views' budget and KVM's dirty log taken out; clock is the interrupt
  time and the precise system file time; threads use priorities.
- GuestRamFile's file is os::RamFile: OwnedFd on Unix, a section on
  Windows; gpu::writes::Keeping is built on Windows too.

Verified: cargo check -p reims-vgpu-vulkan on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
(0 errors, 6 warnings). Not run yet: the Linux tests copied with the
modules are cfg'd off until the Windows ones are written; no VM boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
